// Butcher's weight — a brutal counterweight: adds base damage (heavier hits). GTW-549
// data-driven attachment ITEM (the grimdark "ButchersWeight" tag). Referenced by a weapon BY
// KEY in its `attachments:` list; applied post-spawn. (The GTW-542 tag also slowed the
// weapon's fire modes; that slower-fire coupling is a USER-REVIEW composite — the shipped
// default is the damage bump alone.)
(
    display_name: "Butcher's Weight",
    // GTW-554: the MELEE counterweight example — occupies the Counterweight socket, so it fits
    // only a melee weapon declaring one (a ranged weapon declares Muzzle/Sight/Rail and REJECTS
    // it; class gating emerges from the slots, never from a class tag).
    slot: Counterweight,
    effects: [
        Damage(4),  // +4 to the weapon's base damage — tunable
    ],
)
